Response:
"Just anxiety" doesn't cause sleeping 0 hours in 4 days. I suspect your GP assumes you are not actually getting zero sleep. Patients often say they get no sleep when they in fact do get some sleep. It can help to keep a sleep journal, so that you can clearly communicate to your GP how much sleep you got.

&#x200B;

Are you using any stimulants? Caffeine?

&#x200B;

Do not drive in this condition.

